       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Per dose:** 1600 mg is double the usual maximum single dose of ibuprofen, which is 800 mg.\n- **Per day:** 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. The maximum is 3,200 mg/day in a monitored setting, and 2,400 mg/day is more typical. At 6,400 mg/day the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- 400 mg PO four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n- 600 mg PO four times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- 1,600 mg total per day, split into smaller doses\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. I'd also suggest you review it with pharmacy."
      }
     ],
